From 1de1e319b1fbc2d77b9825735d0dd1a10982561f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:59:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] l2r-local: bug 17: lower SCF to ControlFlow without pattern
 rollback

rrc's memory grew with the square of the length of a straight-line
function on lean2rr's `Nat` (a value enum: every operation is a match, so
after ConvertToSTD a block of N `scf.if`/`scf.index_switch`): 0.43 GB for
250 `let`s, 1.17 GB for 500, 4.1 GB for 1000, out of memory at 14 GB for
2500. The peak was reached in `convert-scf-to-cf`.

MLIR's stock pass runs its patterns through the dialect conversion driver,
which records every operation a pattern moves so that it can roll the
conversion back. Lowering an `scf.if` (a switch, a loop) moves the rest of
its block into a new block, so a block of N of them records N^2/2 moves:
16000 `scf.if` in one block take 8.4 s and 9.3 GB in reussir-opt
`--convert-scf-to-cf`.

Create the pass with `allowPatternRollback = false`, the option upstream
offers for this pass: the same patterns, applied without the record. The
same block takes 1.0 s and 142 MB, and the output is identical.

Measured on lean2rr's output for reussir-bugs/repros/bug17-long-nat-block.py
(L2R_NO_OUTLINE=1, rrc time and peak memory): 250 lets: 19 s, 427 MB ->
19 s, 318 MB; 500: 30 s, 1.17 GB -> 27 s, 610 MB; 1000: 57 s, 4.1 GB ->
53 s, 0.95 GB; 2000 (did not build before): 134 s, 1.7 GB. The LLVM IR
rrc emits is identical (up to the random names of texture modules) for
the 18 programs of lean2rr's classic corpus and four lean2rr repros; the
lit suite passes.
---
 lib/CAPI/Passes.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/CAPI/Passes.cpp b/lib/CAPI/Passes.cpp
index 0a578cff..cdc024ef 100644
--- a/lib/CAPI/Passes.cpp
+++ b/lib/CAPI/Passes.cpp
@@ -201,7 +201,14 @@ MlirPass reussirCreateControlFlowSinkPass(void) {
   return wrapOwned(mlir::createControlFlowSinkPass());
 }
 MlirPass reussirCreateSCFToControlFlowPass(void) {
-  return wrapOwned(mlir::createSCFToControlFlowPass());
+  // Without rollback: the conversion driver otherwise records every operation
+  // a pattern moves, and lowering an `scf.if` (or a switch, or a loop) moves
+  // the rest of its block, so a block of N of them took time and memory
+  // quadratic in N. Upstream offers the mode for this pass; its patterns
+  // check what they need before they change the IR.
+  mlir::SCFToControlFlowPassOptions options;
+  options.allowPatternRollback = false;
+  return wrapOwned(mlir::createSCFToControlFlowPass(options));
 }
 MlirPass reussirCreateExpandStridedMetadataPass(void) {
   return wrapOwned(mlir::memref::createExpandStridedMetadataPass());
-- 
